ith a particle of  a given momentum and then in this  experiment by Davisson and Germer  they actually find that electrons  through what amounts to a double slit  behave like particles whose wavelength  is indeed given by this number H divided  by the momentum of the particles  confirming the idea that debris had put  forward so this is a giant step forward  in the trajectory toward the quantum  laws of physics there are a few vital  steps still to go that we will cover in  subsequent episodes but this profound  formula that comes from dubrow that the  wave length comes from H over P is a key  step in that progression and will carry  on in subsequent episodes with the  Schrodinger equation and the  probabilistic interpretation of quantum  mechanics all that is coming up but for  today that's all I wanted to say so  until next time take care this is your  daily equation
 

